--- api 1-180 ---
   1: # API reference
   2: 
   3: The public surface is everything exported from `lib/wenz_richtext.dart`. APIs
   4: are tagged in three stability tiers (see the library doc comment for the full
   5: tier list); this page groups them by module for quick lookup and shows the
   6: typical call shape. For the layered design behind these types, see
   7: `architecture.md`.
   8: 
   9: ## Model layer (tier 1)
  10: 
  11: | Type | Purpose |
  12: | --- | --- |
  13: | `RichTextDocument` | Top-level document: `version` + ordered `BlockNode` list + optional `CommentThread` / `RevisionChange` lists. JSON-round-trippable via the codecs. |
  14: | `BlockNode` (abstract) + concrete subclasses | `TextBlockNode` (paragraph/heading/quote/listItem), `CodeBlockNode`, `ImageBlockNode`, `VideoBlockNode`, `BlockEmbedNode`, `FileBlockNode`, `DividerBlockNode`, `CalloutBlockNode`, `TableBlockNode`. Immutable; `copy()` / `toJson()` / `fromJson()`. `BlockEmbedNode` stores `embedType/data/fallbackText` for business-owned block embeds; `FileBlockNode` stores `assetId/name/size/file` plus `mimeType/downloadUrl/uploadStatus/uploadError`. |
  15: | `InlineNode` | `TextRun(text, attributes)` and `InlineEmbed(embedType, data, attributes)` (link/formula/mention/emoji/image). |
  16: | `FileUploadStatus` | Attachment workflow state: `none`, `pending`, `uploading`, `uploaded`, `failed`; JSON stores the string name when not `none`. |
  17: | `TextAttributes` / `BlockAttributes` | Inline run attributes (bold/italic/color/url/commentIds/revisionIds/…) and block attributes (level/indent/alignment/listType/checked/childNote/anchor). |
  18: | `CommentAnchor` / `CommentThread` / `CommentEntry` | Comment-thread model: stores selection-compatible anchors, author/time/message payloads, and `open` / `resolved` status. |
  19: | `RevisionRange` / `RevisionChange` | Revision model: stores selection-compatible ranges, insert/delete/format type, pending/accepted/rejected status, author/time payloads, and optional before/after format attributes. |
  20: | `DocumentVersionSnapshot` | Application-owned version snapshot: deep-copied `RichTextDocument` plus id/time/author/description, optional `baseSnapshotId` for future diff flows, and JSON-compatible metadata. |
  21: | `TableModel` / `TableCellNode` | Table structure: rows/columns/spans/header/bg/width. |
  22: | `DocumentSchema` | Canonical document normaliser; invariants enforced on every command and load. |
  23: | `DocumentPosition` / `DocumentSelection` / `PositionPath` | Selection contract — three position shapes (block text, block code, table cell) plus structured sort. |
  24: 
  25: `ImageBlockNode` carries `assetId`/`file`, natural `width`/`height`, display
  26: `showWidth`/`showHeight`, plus `caption` and `altText`. JSON writes
  27: `altText` and also reads a legacy/external `alt` key for compatibility.
  28: 
  29: `BlockEmbedNode` is the generic business block embed model. It JSON round-trips
  30: `embedType`, JSON-compatible `data`, and `fallbackText`; HTML preserves these
  31: through `data-wenz-block="embed"`, while Markdown/plain text export a readable
  32: fallback line.
  33: 
  34: `CalloutBlockNode` carries inline `content`, a canonical `variant`
  35: (`info`/`success`/`warning`/`danger`), and optional custom `title`/`icon`.
  36: When `title` or `icon` is empty, renderers and Markdown/HTML export use the
  37: variant default through `effectiveTitle` / `effectiveIcon`.
  38: 
  39: ## Commands (tier 1 / tier 2 / tier 3)
  40: 
  41: All mutations are `EditorCommand` objects routed through `CommandExecutor`.
  42: 
  43: - **Text (tier 1):** `InsertTextCommand`, `DeleteBackwardCommand`,
  44:   `DeleteForwardCommand`, `DeleteSelectionCommand`, `EnterCommand`.
  45:   `EnterCommand` extends list items when the current item is non-empty and
  46:   exits the list when the current list item is empty; task-list continuations
  47:   start unchecked.
  48: - **Style (tier 1):** `FormatTextCommand`, `ClearStyleCommand`,
  49:   `SetBlockTypeCommand`, `SetAlignmentCommand`.
  50: - **Inline (tier 2):** `SetLinkCommand`, `AutoLinkUrlsCommand`,
