 329: 
 330: `AutoSaveState` exposes `status`, `isDirty`, `revision`, `lastChangedAt`,
 331: `lastSaveAttemptAt`, `lastSavedAt`, and `error`. `AutoSaveSnapshot` passes the
 332: document, rich JSON, local revision, and change time to the persistence adapter.
 333: Successful saves mark the current snapshot clean; failed saves keep dirty state
 334: and expose the error for UI retry affordances.
 335: 
 336: `DocumentVersionSnapshot` (tier 2) is the version-history storage unit for host
 337: apps. It stores a deep-copied document plus `id`, `createdAt`, optional
 338: `authorId` / `authorName`, `description`, `baseSnapshotId`, and JSON-compatible
 339: `metadata`; the snapshot list remains outside `RichTextDocument`.
 340: 
 341: ```dart
 342: final snapshot = controller.createVersionSnapshot(
 343:   id: 'v1',
 344:   authorName: 'Ada',
 345:   description: 'Before publishing',
 346:   baseSnapshotId: 'draft-v0', // optional future diff anchor
 347: );
 348: 
 349: const snapshotCodec = DocumentVersionSnapshotJsonCodec();
 350: final payload = snapshotCodec.encode(snapshot);
 351: final restored = snapshotCodec.decode(payload);
 352: controller.restoreVersionSnapshot(restored);
 353: ```
