 355: ## Collaboration adapter layer (tier 2)
 356: 
 357: | Type | Purpose |
 358: | --- | --- |
 359: | `WenzCollaborationAdapter` | App-owned collaboration backend bridge. Implementations publish local document changes / local selection and expose remote document / remote selection streams. |
 360: | `WenzCollaborationController` | Optional sidecar controller that observes `WenzRichTextController` via `addListener`, publishes local mutations, applies remote document snapshots without echo, and exposes remote selections for renderer layers. |
 361: | `WenzLocalDocumentChange` | Local change event containing `clientId`, current `RichTextDocument`, rich JSON snapshot, local revision, change time, selection, and `changedBlockIds`. |
 362: | `WenzRemoteDocumentUpdate` | Backend-resolved remote document snapshot with optional transformed local selection and history-clear policy. |
 363: | `WenzRemoteSelectionUpdate` | Ephemeral remote cursor/selection or clear event. It round-trips JSON for transport payloads and reports `isCursor` / `isClear`. |
 364: | `WenzCollaborationPeer` | Lightweight peer metadata for labels, avatars, and cursor colors. |
 365: 
 366: ```dart
 367: final collaboration = WenzCollaborationController(
 368:   editor: controller,
 369:   adapter: myCollaborationAdapter,
 370:   localClientId: 'client-a',
 371:   localPeer: const WenzCollaborationPeer(
 372:     id: 'user-a',
 373:     displayName: 'Alice',
 374:   ),
 375: );
 376: 
 377: final remoteSelections = collaboration.remoteSelections;
 378: ```
 379: 
 380: The collaboration API does not store presence, cursors, selections, rooms, or
 381: backend metadata in `RichTextDocument`. It does not bind the package to Yjs,
 382: CRDT, OT, WebSocket, or a server implementation; adapters own that translation.
 383: 
 384: ## Codec & migration layer (tier 2)
 385: 
 386: | Type | Purpose |
 387: | --- | --- |
 388: | `RichTextJsonCodec({migrations})` | Encode/decode the canonical versioned rich JSON. Optional `DocumentMigrationRegistry` lifts older versions. |
 389: | `LegacyWenJsonCodec()` | Decode the old `wenz_editor` block-list format. |
 390: | `PlainTextCodec({omitEmptyBlocks})` | Export to plain text (paragraphs blank-line separated, media sentinels; image sentinel prefers caption, then alt text). |
 391: | `MarkdownCodec()` | GFM Markdown import/export. `encode` → Markdown; `decode` → document (line-oriented state machine; unrecognised lines fall back to paragraphs). Image caption uses Markdown image title: `![alt](src "caption")`; video blocks export/import through the Wenz `![video](src)` placeholder; file and block embed content degrade to readable text/links on import. |
 392: | `HtmlCodec()` | HTML fragment import/export via `package:html`. `encode` → HTML; `decode` → document (DOM walk; malformed HTML falls back to paragraphs). Image block captions use `<figure><img ...><figcaption>...`; inline image embeds preserve `altText`/`caption`/`width`/`height` through `<img>` attributes; Wenz file links, video tags, and `BlockEmbedNode` preserve metadata through `data-*` attributes; table `rowspan`/`colspan` maps to `TableCellNode` spans. |
 393: | `DocumentVersionSnapshotJsonCodec()` | Encode/decode one `DocumentVersionSnapshot` or a snapshot list for app-owned version history persistence. |
 394: | `DocumentMigration` / `DocumentMigrationRegistry` | JSON-level schema migration framework; ships `V1ToV2DocumentMigration`. |
 395: | `decodeWithMigrations(source, registry)` | Helper: JSON decode + migrate in one step. |
 396: | `DocumentDecodeException` | Structured codec error (`reason`, `jsonPath?`, `raw?`). |
 397: | `UnknownCommandException` | Structured error raised by `CommandRegistry.build` for unknown names. |
 398: | `TryLoadResult` | Outcome of `tryLoadJson`: `ok` / `document?` / `error?`. |
 399: | `WenzEditorPermission` | Controller command policy: `read`, `comment`, `edit`. |
 400: 
 401: ## External document conversion plan (tier 2)
 402: 
 403: | Type | Purpose |
 404: | --- | --- |
 405: | `WenzDocumentConversionPlan` | Declarative PDF/DOCX boundary: format, direction, owner, platform families, dependency boundaries, degradation boundaries, and summary. |
 406: | `wenzDocumentConversionPlans` / `wenzDocumentConversionPlanFor(format, direction)` | Default ADV-022 matrix for PDF export/import and DOCX export/import. All entries keep PDF/DOCX runtime dependencies outside this package. |
 407: | `WenzDocumentExporter<TOutput>` | App-owned export adapter contract. Implementations receive a `RichTextDocument` and return bytes, files, URLs, or another app-defined output type. |
 408: | `WenzDocumentImporter<TSource>` | App-owned import adapter contract. Implementations receive app-defined DOCX/source input and return a `RichTextDocument`. PDF import is explicitly unsupported by the default plan. |
 409: 
 410: PDF/DOCX conversion is not wired into `WenzRichTextController`: host apps choose
 411: their PDF renderer, print pipeline, OOXML package, native plugin, or server
 412: worker and call the adapter from their own UI. See `import_export_strategy.md`
 413: for the platform, dependency, asset, and degradation boundaries.
 414: 
 415: For contributor-facing schema evolution rules, see
 416: `schema_migration_impact.md`. Public API additions that alter persisted rich
 417: JSON must document whether they reuse the current schema, add optional fields,
 418: or require a new `DocumentMigration` step.
 419: 
